{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDIwL015JTIwRGFkcyUyMENocmlzdG1hcyUyMERhdGUlMjAlMjgyMDIwJTI5Lw","type":"movie","name":"My Dads Christmas Date","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/mAfeEGYIwEG4YmVk77pv8fk0Dpr.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/aAm4qRCzWB9l5XTuuCdrhNpiyyH.jpg","description":"It’s Christmas and the charming city of York, home to Jules, 16, and her dad, David, is decked out ready for the festive season. In many ways, David and Jules’ relationship is no different from that of most fathers and their sixteen-year-old daughters. He struggles to understand her, she refuses to communicate with him. He wants to be involved in her life, she wants her own space. In one important respect, however, David and Jules share a profound bond: the death of Jules’ mum, and David’s wife, in a car crash two years before. With both struggling to cope with everyday life in the shadow of their loss, Jules, inspired by happy memories of her mum, decides to take matters into her own hands.\n\nRated NR · Released 3 Dec 2020 · United Kingdom · Language: English · 91 min\nStudio: Goldfinch, Highfield Grange Studios, SPI International\n\nOn your server — Audio: English · Subtitle files: English","releaseInfo":"2020","genres":["Romance","Comedy","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"6.2","runtime":"91 min","cast":["Jeremy Piven","Olivia-Mai Barrett","Hadar Cats","Joely Richardson","Megan Brown Martinez","Felix Butterwick","Sophie Corcoran","Janine Craig"],"director":["Mick Davis"],"released":"2020-12-03T00:00:00.000Z","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Mick Davis","character":"Director"},{"name":"Jeremy Piven","character":"David","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/pBD1jcAZiDrHWcFpJtBtqLRD4gR.jpg"},{"name":"Olivia-Mai Barrett","character":"Jules","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/gWZRzvOnUxZmvdzHuxBvIS0BEJP.jpg"},{"name":"Hadar Cats","character":"Emma","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/jIDjjQ7yBkMYhZ6HC0e4Cshr